World "DataStructures"
Title "Data Structures"

Introduction "Data structures carry invariants, not just shapes: a binary
search tree keeps its keys ordered, an AVL tree keeps its height balanced,
a chained hash table keeps every key discoverable through its bucket, and
a union-find structure keeps path compression invisible to its
representatives."
